{"entityType": "recommendation", "canonicalName": "Low Blood Sugar Emergency Response", "properties": {"statement": "If I am acting strangely or cannot be awakened, my blood sugar may be low. If I cannot be awakened or cannot swallow, do not try to give me anything by mouth. Please contact Emergency Medical Services (911) immediately. If I can swallow, give me 4 to 6 ounces of fruit juice, sweetened soft drink, or other sugar source. If I am not better within 10-15 minutes, contact Emergency Medical Services (911) immediately.", "recommendationType": "Safety", "populationScope": "People with diabetes who are experiencing symptoms of low blood sugar", "nativeEvidenceGrade": "Unspecified", "gradingSystem": "VA-DoD", "recommendationStrength": "Strong"}, "relations": [], "quote": "If I am acting strangely or cannot be awakened, my blood sugar may be low.  If I cannot be awakened or cannot swallow, do not try to give me anything by mouth. Please contact Emergency Medical Services (911) immediately.  If I can swallow, give me 4 to 6 ounces of fruit juice, sweetened soft drink, or other sugar source. If I am not better within 10-15 minutes, contact Emergency Medical Services (911) immediately.", "propertyEvidence": {}, "chunkIndex": 0}
